Weighted Mean
During the data collection process, this statistical tool will be used to calculate the weighted values of the questionnaire responses provided by the respondents. The formula for the weighted mean is as follows:
		 	
	




Where:
Xˉ = weighted mean (average score)
x = score or weight of each response ( 1 = Strongly Disagree, 2 = Disagree, 3 = Agree, 4 = Strongly Agree)
f = frequency of respondents choosing that score
∑(f⋅x) = sum of all products of frequency × weight
∑f = total number of respondents
The formula calculates the average by multiplying each response’s weight by its frequency, summing the resulting products, and dividing by the total number of respondents. 


Standard Deviation 
	Standard deviation is a statistical measure that indicates how much the scores in a data set vary from the mean, helping researchers assess the consistency and significance of the differences between pre-test and post-test results.
						
Where:
	σ = Standard Deviation
	∑ = Summation Symbol
	x = Individual Score
	μ = Average of the Scores
	N = Total Number of Scores

